<p id="_bd0a2c9e-61d5-5a94-1f71-a2c4f6b72885"><underline>Remarks:</underline></p>

<ul id="_c57166bb-d78e-9af4-9f0a-37031a40192f"><li><p id="_02005d3d-ae61-28cc-bf57-e23c04e5a9e9">In addition to using the <strong>typeOfBroadcastContent</strong> attribute, <strong>subjectDescription</strong> attribute may be used to describe the broadcast content of a specific service.</p>
</li>
<li><p id="_96d39edf-d70e-803a-79af-5f72e09e09ad">The <strong>subjectOrMessageTypeCode</strong> is for encoding the subject code or message type specified for the communication system to indicate the transmitted content. For example, message type of DGNSS, subject code for NAVDAT messages or the B<sub>2</sub> character used to indicate the subject group of the maritime safety information (MSI) message. B<sub>2</sub> subject indicator character is used by the MSI receiver to identify the different classes of messages (MSC.1/Circ.1403/Rev.2).</p>
</li>
</ul>

<p id="_9eb6085e-da1e-957b-f37a-bb57a180f838"><underline>Distinction:</underline></p>
